virglrenderer: Venus commands come where Vulkan allows them

What: vkr keeps a little state per command buffer: recording or not, the
render pass or rendering that is open (its subpass, colors and view mask),
whether a graphics or a compute pipeline is bound, conditional rendering. A
command on a command buffer that does not record, a draw outside a pass or
without a graphics pipeline, a dispatch inside a pass or without a compute
pipeline, a clear outside a pass or of a color attachment the subpass lacks,
a pass begun inside another, a next subpass past the last, a pass end
without its begin, a query in a multiview pass past the pool's end for its
views, a conditional rendering end without its begin, vkEndCommandBuffer
with a pass or conditional rendering open, and the execution of a secondary
that still records or does not match the primary's pass end the app's
context.
Why: KosmicKrisp (NDEBUG) ended on a draw or dispatch without a pipeline, on
a next subpass past the last and on a pass end without a begin (SIGSEGV,
end_subpass); MoltenVK with prefill on the same and on a draw outside a pass
(SIGSEGV at vkEndCommandBuffer).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (spec VUIDs), draft only.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the c-state- cases).

